    {
      "diff": "@@ -995,3 +995,45 @@ i.e., the file 'wireshark-disable-versioning' must exist in the git repo dir.\n  * vi: set shiftwidth=4 tabstop=8 expandtab:\n  * :indentSize=4:tabSize=8:noTabs=true:\n  */\n+\n+\n+== Restoring Fork Relationship on GitLab\n+\n+If your fork is no longer linked to the upstream Wireshark repository on GitLab (for example, after a migration), you may not be able to create Merge Requests.\n+\n+To fix this, follow these steps:\n+\n+1. Go to any GitLab page (e.g., this issue).\n+2. Open the **Developer Console** in your browser:\n+   - Firefox: `Ctrl+Shift+K` (or `Cmd+Option+K` on macOS)\n+   - Chrome: `Ctrl+Shift+J` (or `Cmd+Option+J` on macOS)\n+\n+3. Paste and run the following JavaScript snippet:\n+\n+[source,javascript]\n+----\n+alert(await (async () => {\n+  let project_name = 'wireshark';\n+  let project_id = 7898047;\n+  let token = document.querySelector('meta[name=csrf-token]').content;\n+  if (!gon.current_username) return 'Not logged in or not on gitlab.com?';\n+  else if (!token) return 'auth token not found';\n+  // Remove existing (broken) fork relationship if any.\n+  await fetch(`https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/${gon.current_username}%2F${project_name}/fork`, {\n+    method: 'DELETE',\n+    headers: { 'x-csrf-token': token }\n+  });\n+  // Reset fork relationship\n+  let r = await fetch(`https://gitlab.com/api/v4/projects/${gon.current_username}%2F${project_name}/fork/${project_id}`, {\n+    method: 'POST',\n+    headers: { 'x-csrf-token': token }\n+  });\n+  if (r.status !== 201) return `Error ${r.status} ${await r.text()}`;\n+  return 'Everything should be OK!';\n+})());\n+----\n+\n+If successful, you’ll see a pop-up saying: **Everything should be OK!**\n+\n+This script uses the GitLab API to reset the fork relationship. It’s safe to use while logged into your GitLab account and only affects your own fork.\n+\n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "doc/README.developer",
